# shadcn/ui — Mandatory UI Library

**shadcn/ui is the ONLY permitted UI library in this project.** There are zero exceptions.

- **No custom UI components.** Do not create bespoke styled divs, hand-rolled form controls, or any other custom UI primitives. Every visible UI element must be composed from shadcn/ui components.
- **No raw HTML elements** (`<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<dialog>`, etc.) when a shadcn/ui equivalent exists.
- **No other component libraries** (MUI, Chakra, Radix primitives imported directly, Headless UI, etc.).

If a shadcn/ui component does not yet cover a use case, open a discussion rather than inventing a custom component.

**MANDATORY Rules:**
- ❌ NEVER create custom buttons, inputs, cards, modals, or any UI elements
- ❌ NEVER use raw HTML elements (div, button, input) for UI
- ❌ NEVER write custom CSS for components beyond Tailwind utilities
- ✅ ALWAYS use shadcn/ui components for every UI element
- ✅ ALWAYS compose complex UI by combining shadcn/ui components
- ✅ This project is in dark mode so make sure there are no dark colored text on dark backgrounds (and vice versa)

## Clerk Authentication UI

Clerk's built-in `<SignInButton>` and `<SignUpButton>` components **must** render as shadcn/ui `<Button>` elements using the `asChild` prop. Sign-in and sign-up flows **must** open in a Clerk modal — never navigate to a dedicated sign-in/sign-up page.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — shadcn Button + Clerk modal
import { SignInButton, SignUpButton } from "@clerk/nextjs";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

<SignInButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Sign in</Button>
</SignInButton>

<SignUpButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Sign up</Button>
</SignUpButton>

// ❌ BAD — Clerk's default anchor/button styling
<SignInButton />

// ❌ BAD — navigates away instead of using modal
<SignInButton mode="redirect">
  <Button>Sign in</Button>
</SignInButton>
```

## Initialization

If shadcn/ui is not yet set up in the project, run:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

## Adding Components

Before using a component, check whether it is already installed under `components/ui/`. If it is not, add it with:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>
```

Example — adding the Button component:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
```

## Usage

Import components from the local `components/ui/` path, not from an npm package:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

// ❌ BAD
import { Button } from "shadcn-ui";
```
